sted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284313-converting-nanomachine-swarms-to-sorcery?p=1284729#post1284729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Duh. It's a cloud of nanites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon me if I'm still unconvinced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284313-converting-nanomachine-swarms-to-sorcery?p=1284355#post1284355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rules wise it hasn't been able to do that since 1e and &quot;two Sidereals murdered everyone in Fallen Lapis&quot; got retconned into House Tepet razing the city.<br /> <br /> Edit: Summoning the Heart of Darkness was actually the Celestial Circle 'city killer' in 2e because it plunged a mile into a zone of darkness where people not only couldn't see but also couldn't hear anything besides screams. In 3e it's been replaced with Impenetrable Veil of Night which is still terrifying but less likely to make people respond to this terror by attacking their own loved ones reaching for them in the darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHm, didn't see this post before - forum glitch?<br /> <br /> Anyway, yeah, completely overlooked Impenetrable Veil of Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T01:15:20-08:00","id":1285154,"title":"","content":"Fine. Non airtight armour. Just stunt it was the nanites crawling through the gaps in the plating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T02:10:12-08:00","id":1285165,"title":"","content":"Armour doesn't normally help against environmental damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284313-converting-nanomachine-swarms-to-sorcery?p=1284943#post1284943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bHm, didn't see this post before - forum glitch?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? Edits can be pretty slow appearing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T10:07:00-08:00","id":1285276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284313-converting-nanomachine-swarms-to-sorcery?p=1284943#post1284943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pardon me if I'm still unconvinced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, pardon me for not caring about your suspension of disbelief. Its a cloud of nanites conjured by sorcery. It can do whatever it wants, as long as it isn't unbalanced over overpowered? <br /> <br /> Another thing.<br /> <br /> Don't. Act. Like. A. Prick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T10:26:27-08:00","id":1285284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284313-converting-nanomachine-swarms-to-sorcery?p=1285276#post1285276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't. Act. Like. A. Prick.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Or indeed, address your fellow forum members this way. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T03:26:48-07:00","id":1297674,"title":"","content":"Necroing this thread since I just watched the season finale. Any thoughts on how Nemesis used the nanos in the end?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T03:37:34-07:00","id":1297678,"title":"","content":"It looked like sorcery/necromancy/weaving to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T06:41:13-07:00","id":1297707,"title":"","content":"actually, something to do with it. <br /> <br /> I've got an idea after reading Conan: The Avenger. He once said that Thoth Amon could transform men's blood into scarabs. <br /> <br /> So... an idea from that: <br /> <br /> An attack that transform's people blood into scarabs, up to medium range, leading them to eat their way out of the victims bodies and burst into the air. They can increase their numbers by feeding on other people, transforming the blood that spurts out into more blood scarabs. This isn't perfect, and eventually the swarm will hit a limit, but its pretty darned horrifying.<br /> <br /> So the question is, how does one depict and mechanically calculate swarms in 3e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T07:30:36-07:00","id":1297715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284313-converting-nanomachine-swarms-to-sorcery?p=1297707#post1297707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">actually, something to do with it.<br /> <br /> I've got an idea after reading Conan: The Avenger. He once said that Thoth Amon could transform men's blood into scarabs.<br /> <br /> So... an idea from that:<br /> <br /> An attack that transform's people blood into scarabs, up to medium range, leading them to eat their way out of the victims bodies and burst into the air. They can increase their numbers by feeding on other people, transforming the blood that spurts out into more blood scarabs. This isn't perfect, and eventually the swarm will hit a limit, but its pretty darned horrifying.<br /> <br /> So the question is, how does one depict and mechanically calculate swarms in 3e?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is powerful. Blood of Boiling Oil is similarly lethal and a good baseline to use.<br /> Swarms...the Dune Swarm is the one i remember right now. It is a single creature sheet, composed of hundreds or thousands of little creepy crawlies.<br /> <br /> The merits that relate directly to it being a swarm give...<br /> Minimum withering damage against it is one less than normal, it ignores difficult terrain, has an automatic success for most combat actions (attack, movement, sensors against ambushes).<br /> When it is controlling a grapple, missed attacks automatically aim at their target, and its decisive attack deals +1 damage against lower initiative enemies (a success instead of a die for crashed enemies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 03-18-2019, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T07:58:36-07:00","id":1297723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284313-converting-nanomachine-swarms-to-sorcery?p=1297715#post1297715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is powerful. Blood of Boiling Oil is similarly lethal and a good baseline to use.<br /> Swarms...the Dune Swarm is the one i remember right now. It is a single creature sheet, composed of hundreds or thousands of little creepy crawlies.<br /> <br /> The merits that relate directly to it being a swarm give...<br /> Minimum withering damage against it is one less than normal, it ignores difficult terrain, has an automatic success for most combat actions (attack, movement, sensors against ambushes).<br /> When it is controlling a grapple, missed attacks automatically aim at their target, and its decisive attack deals +1 damage against lower initiative enemies (a success instead of a die for crashed enemies).</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember someone making a demon that was a swarm. <br /> <br /> Reduced damage for singular attacks. Increased damage for AoE attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T08:29:03-07:00","id":1297731,"title":"","content":"That's a way to go about it. Flight of Separation makes you a swarm. It gives you evasion against non-aoe attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T08:47:11-07:00","id":1297733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284313-converting-nanomachine-swarms-to-sorcery?p=1297731#post1297731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a way to go about it. Flight of Separation makes you a swarm. It gives you evasion against non-aoe attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But how does one mechanically express the ever growing swarm mechanic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T09:23:41-07:00","id":1297740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284313-converting-nanomachine-swarms-to-sorcery?p=1297733#post1297733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. But how does one mechanically express the ever growing swarm mechanic?</div> </div> </div> </div>battle groups/ multiple attacks and ST fiat","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11701-fiikragg","name":"Fiikragg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T09:50:52-07:00","id":1297749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fiikragg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1284313-converting-nanomachine-swarms-to-sorcery?p=1297740#post1297740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> battle groups/ multiple attacks and ST fiat</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.... I don't know about that. I've looked at battlegroups. Its all confusing to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T10:07:53-07:00","id":1297755,"title":"","content":"You may want to get better acquainted with the system before making additions and modifications to it, then.<br /> <br /> Battlegroups have an inflated character sheet over their average member, mainly by virtue of Size.<br /> <br /> Their attacks are all withering attacks, but they damage your life if you're crashed and they don't gain or lose initiative.<br /> Withering attacks against them don't give you initiative for the damage (but do for hitting and for crashing/zeroing magnitude). Decisive attacks against them deal a lot of extra damage automatically.<br /> <br /> You can command them to inflate their attack or restore lost magnitude or prevent routs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}